{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>He will send you from here — like his sending.</b> In the same manner that he already sent you and Aaron from his presence in wrath, as it says: וַיְגָרֶשׁ אֹתָם מֵאֵת פְּנֵי פַרְעֹה (Exodus 10:11) — in that same manner he will now send you, compelled by his distress." "<b>Completely — he will drive you out.</b> But then he drove out only the two of you, and only from his presence. Now, however, he will drive all of you out from this entire place. For this is the measure of justice of the Holy One, blessed be He: when a man stubbornly refrains from doing what is fitting instead of doing the will of his Maker, He brings it about that the very thing the man fled from comes upon him in distress and grief, and not of his own will — as it says: תַּחַת אֲשֶׁר לֹא עָבַדְתָּ (Deuteronomy 28:47), וְעָבַדְתָּ אֶת אֹיְבֶיךָ (Deuteronomy 28:48); אִם לֹא כַּאֲשֶׁר דִּבַּרְתֶּם בְּאָזְנַי כֵּן אֶעֱשֶׂה לָכֶם (Numbers 14:28); as the Sages said: הַמְבַטֵּל אֶת הַתּוֹרָה מֵעֹשֶׁר, סוֹפוֹ לְבַטְּלָהּ מֵעֹנִי (Mishnah Avot 4:10)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:09.211515564Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}